  "The Canon Against Surplusage: Unanimously recognized across both camps as fatal to the static 38 interpretation. Only the dynamic model gives operative meaning to: (a) inclusion of DC and Puerto Rico (defining P_total = 285,230,516); (b) the exact 51-month window (two biennial election cycles from late 2000 through March 2005 to overturn 100% of seats, including staggered 4-year state senates); (c) the prohibition on financial incentives (protecting voluntary migration from vote-buying statutes).",
  "Mathematical and Census Proof: Uniform minimax defense requires P_C/50 per state. Adversary needs strictly > (13/50)*P_C to capture 13 states. Condition: P_C > (50/63)*P_total (~79.36508%). For Census 2000 P_total = 285,230,516, the cutoff is 226,373,425.4. Cumulative population of top 22 states is 222,190,310; adding 23rd state (Alabama, 4,447,100) reaches 226,637,410, strictly crossing the threshold."
],
"current_stance": "23 is mathematically and constitutionally certain. The group is on the verge of unanimous consensus (15/18 already voting 23, the remaining 3 essentially conceding). In Round 3, I will welcome the final convergence on 23."
}

