  "38": "Permanently rejected. Static institutional roll-call model violates verba cum effectu sunt accipienda by rendering DC, Puerto Rico, the 51-month timeline, and the financial incentive ban superfluous.",
  "5 / 9 / 26 / 34": "Previously eliminated as mathematically incomplete, neglecting adversarial counter-migration, or miscalculating the blocking threshold."
},
"critical_syntheses_and_resolutions": [
  "Canon Against Surplusage: Every specific parameter in the prompt has operative force only under the dynamic model: (1) DC + PR explicitly included (and other territories excluded) to set the closed national demographic universe of mobile citizens at P_total = 285,230,516; (2) 51-month clock from anywhere in 2000 (worst case: Dec 31, 2000) extends to March 31, 2005, spanning exactly two biennial general elections (Nov 2002, Nov 2004) plus 3 months for swearing-in to democratically overturn 100% of seats in staggered 4-year state senates; (3) 'No financial incentives' aligns with federal anti-vote-buying statutes while protecting voluntary ideological relocation under Saenz v. Roe.",
  "Resolution of Candidate Durational Residency: Triply resolved under standing law: (1) Native Candidate Mobilization: single-minded voting majorities can sponsor and elect qualified local native residents who already satisfy all candidate residency rules; (2) Article V State Ratifying Conventions (United States v. Sprague, Hawke v. Smith): convention delegates exercise a federal constitutional function and are chosen on popular ballots under general voter franchise standards (Dunn v. Blumstein 30-day ceiling), bypassing state legislative candidate qualification rules; (3) 51-Month Timeline: allows early migrants nearly 4 full years of continuous domicile by November 2004, satisfying even the strictest state legislative candidate residency rules nationwide.",
  "Game-Theoretic Minimax Formulation: Article V requires 38 states to ratify (and 34 to compel a convention). Adversary needs 13 states to block (50 - 38 + 1 = 13). Leaving any state unpopulated allows the adversary to take it for free. Minimax defense allocates P_C / 50 across all 50 states. Adversary cost to win 13 states is strictly greater than (13/50) * P_C. Coalition guarantees victory against arbitrary opposition if P_total - P_C < (13/50) * P_C <=> P_C > (50/63) * P_total (~79.36508%).",
  "Census 2000 Demographic Arithmetic: P_total = 281,421,906 (50 States + DC) + 3,808,610 (PR) = 285,230,516. Minimax threshold: (50/63) * 285,230,516 = 226,373,425.4 (requires 226,373,426). Cumulative population of top 22 states (California through Louisiana) = 222,190,310 (insufficient by ~4.18M). Adding the 23rd state (Alabama, 4,447,100) yields 226,637,410 (strictly exceeds threshold by 263,984)."
],
"current_stance": "23 is the mathematically, textually, and legally proven solution. Maintain and reinforce 23 through subsequent rounds to final convergence."
}

